\description{
Cleans the horizontal position (\code{lon}, \code{lat}) of a GNSS stream and adds red
flags for readings that are physically implausible. This is the third step
of the pipeline, after \code{\link[=read_stream]{read_stream()}} and \code{\link[=uniform_stream]{uniform_stream()}} and before
\code{\link[=resample_stream]{resample_stream()}}.

\strong{Red flags} are computed on the raw values, before smoothing, and returned
as logical columns:\tabular{lll}{
   flag \tab rule \tab acts on \cr
   \code{flag_coord} \tab missing coordinate, |lat| > 90, |lon| > 180 or (0, 0) \tab position \cr
   \code{flag_time} \tab time does not increase (\code{delta_t <= 0}) \tab position \cr
   \code{flag_speed} \tab horizontal speed from the previous reading > \code{v_max}, or above the Tobler ceiling when \code{tobler} is given \tab position \cr
   \code{flag_accel} \tab |acceleration| > \code{accel_max} \tab position \cr
   \code{flag_jump} \tab displacement > \code{edge_jump} among the first or last 3 readings \tab position \cr
   \code{flag_slope} \tab |slope| > \code{slope_max} \tab elevation \cr
   \code{flag_vert_speed} \tab |vertical speed| > \code{vert_speed_max} \tab elevation \cr
   \code{flag_idle_ele} \tab elevation changes while the horizontal position does not \tab elevation \cr
   \code{flag_gap} \tab \code{delta_t > gap} \tab information only \cr
   \code{flag_low_res} \tab distance from the previous reading > \code{low_res} \tab information only \cr
}


