In \code{"pipeline"}, a reading is an outlier when at least two of three criteria
hold for any of the derived variables: (1) extreme value, outside
\verb{[Q1 - 1.5 IQR, Q3 + 1.5 IQR]}; (2) abrupt jump, absolute change from the
previous reading larger than \code{jump_k} standard deviations of the changes;
(3) local deviation, distance to the moving mean (window \code{window}) larger than
\code{local_k} moving standard deviations. The paper reports the thresholds
(window 25, jump 1.5, local deviation 2.0, Savitzky-Golay 9/2, edge jump
30 m) but not their exact formulation; the formulation above is the one
implemented here. The uniform temporal interpolation of the paper is not
applied, because spatial resampling (\code{\link[=resample_stream]{resample_stream()}}) follows in the
metrictrails pipeline.
